    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Lawrence Butler**, who commands our highest efficiency score at 74.61. His pairing against Wesneski provides an ideal environment, bolstered by a significant dynamic platoon advantage and a premium spot in the #2 hole. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a core piece with a 68.84 score; despite some BvP inefficiency against Wacha, his inherent talent floor and prime lineup position make him an automatic start. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** (64.17) benefits from the high-upside matchup against Johnson, where his power profile outweighs the minor platoon discount. We are also looking for a rebound performance from **Jonathan Aranda** (62.95) and **Zack Gelof** (62.75), both of whom are positioned to exploit favorable SP xERAs of 3.90 and 4.59, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Justin Crawford** (49.28). While his elite sprint speed remains a priority for our SB-starved roster, his placement in the #9 hole against the capable Jax creates a volatility risk that pushes him below our marginal threshold. With **Bryce Harper** (60.81) and **Will Smith** (60.58) offering more reliable, high-xwOBA production, we are prioritizing floor over the potential for a singular stolen base today. While **Luis Arraez** remains unavailable, his absence from the lineup continues to emphasize our reliance on players like **Lawrence Butler** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** to drive our AVG and R categories. \n\nRisks are relatively contained, though investors should monitor the lineup status for **Cal Raleigh**, as his projection remains sensitive to late-game adjustments. We are also keeping a close eye on the bench, where prospects like **Dylan Beavers**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Braden Montgomery** remain on standby should our active outfielders underperform against the day\u2019s RHP-heavy slate. We are currently navigating around the long-term absences of **Matt Chapman** and **Daulton Varsho**, while **Tyler Freeman** remains in the minors, further thinning our bench utility.",
